Subject: [PATCH] DXGI present: the presenting device waits for each picture's unlock (TODO 98)

The window's pictures go through two Direct3D 11 devices: GL draws each into a texture of the
interop's device (WGL_NV_DX_interop2: lock, blit, unlock) and a second device copies it into the
swap chain's back buffer and presents. Nothing ordered the second device's copy after the interop
device's work at the unlock, and on AMD's driver (RX 7900 XTX, RX 5700 XT) the copy now and then
read the texture before GL's new picture had reached it: the screen showed the picture that
texture held three presents before - a picture ahead and then the ones before it again, the
user's flicker with the pictures between frames on (measured with a number stamped into each
picture, read back from the back buffer: about 1 present in 7 on the RX 5700 XT, 1 in 20 on the
RX 7900 XTX went back to an older picture; none with the fence).

Now a fence shared by the two devices (ID3D11Fence, Direct3D 11.4): the interop's device signals
it after each unlock and the presenting device's GPU waits for it before the copy - no CPU wait.
PS2X_PRESENT_FENCE=0: as before. Also, before GL draws into one of the three textures again, the
presenting device's last copy out of it must be done (an event query, asked without waiting;
PS2X_PRESENT_READGUARD=0: not waited for). And a checking aid: PS2X_PRESENT_STAMPS=1 reads the
picture-number stamps (the game's TF_NATIVE_STAMP) of every present from what went to the back
buffer; PS2X_PRESENT_CAPTURE=<first>,<count>,<dir> also saves those presents at a quarter size.
